    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0228" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg222"/>

                <head>No. 9.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Smith
                        to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hawaiian Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-02-03"><hi rendition="#italic">February 3, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 3.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to submit to you (copy of) official
                    dispatch of the Provisional Government of Hawaii, received by me yesterday.</p>
                <p>It announces the sending of five commissioners, Hon. L. A. Thurston, W. R.
                    Castle, esq., Hon. W. C. Wilder, C. L. Carter, esq., Hon. Joseph Marsden, to
                    treat with the Government of the United States.</p>
                <p>These gentlemen will arrive in Washington this day, and with your consent, I
                    shall be glad to present them to you to-morrow, at the State Department.</p>
                <p>Renewing assurance of my highest consideration,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Mott Smith.</hi></signed></closer>



